    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me summarize the implementation.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional owner email support so the app satisfies the spec and all tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 acceptance tests green).\n\n**What the spec required:** An owner may include `email`; when present it must be a syntactically valid address, stored/returned lower-cased; reject with 400 when present but invalid.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `email` property (`type: string`, `format: email`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because the OpenAPI generator runs with `performBeanValidation`, `format: email` generates a `@Email` constraint on the DTO, and the generated API interface applies `@Valid` to the request body \u2014 so an invalid email (e.g. `not-an-email`) is rejected with **400** automatically, while a missing email is accepted.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `email` field with `@Column(name = \"email\")` and `@Email`, plus getter/setter and the import. MapStruct maps `email` automatically by name between DTO and entity.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Lower-cased the email before persisting, mirroring the existing telephone-normalization pattern, in both `addOwner` and `updateOwner`.\n\n4. **`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added an `email` column to the `owners` table (the test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema must be explicit).\n\n5. **`db/{hsqldb,mysql}/data.sql`** \u2014 The seed inserts used positional `INSERT ... VALUES`, which broke once a column was added. I gave them explicit column lists so `email` defaults to NULL for seed rows (h2 and postgres already used explicit column lists).\n\nVerified end-to-end: `Test.User@Example.COM` is stored and returned as `test.user@example.com`, invalid emails yield 400, and owners without an email create successfully.",
